Open product work

- Report parser and analysis allocation failures reliably. Summary, text
  scope/source and xref data provenance can silently omit facts; index,
  consumer and coverage collectors can fail without explaining why.
- Handle leading unnamed RAM data containing $ in object output. It currently
  fails with an unlocated anchor error. Keep validation of other initializer
  symbols when discarding data that has no allocation identity.
- Preserve earlier linker outputs when publishing a later output fails.
  The linker stages all files but publishes them independently; the assembler
  already rolls back its requested output set on detected failures.
- Bound rich-analysis expansion of shared aliases. It currently turns shared
  graphs into trees and can consume exponential memory. Text listings avoid
  this path; focus optimization on demonstrated workloads.
- Improve diagnostic-listing availability when FCEUX ROM export is requested
  after a syntax error or unresolved storage. Do not publish a partial set
  when its destinations cannot be planned safely.
- Avoid repeated scans of very long shared-label runs in sizeof, if a real
  workload warrants it. The current synthetic worst case grows cubically.
- Deduplicate size-unknown diagnostics for multiple sizeof uses of one operand.
- Investigate unused-label warnings through constant-alias chains. Keep source
  usage separate from references retained only for export or layout.

Release coordination: design/v2/I6_RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md.
Approved behavior and scope: XORCYST_V2_CONTRACTS.md and XORCYST_V2_DESIGN.md.
Completed implementation history and validation: design/v2/.
